{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-212809",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{8}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{8}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{8}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{8}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}}{8} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we notice that $8$ has a perfect square factor $(4).$ Therefore, we can rewrite $\\sqrt{8}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our original fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3\\cdot 2}}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-212809\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>To remove the radical <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"62\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.163em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"63\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.163em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and simplify:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"64\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 5.364em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.4em;\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-fra